      "comment": "CHAMPAGNE WALSH (7) scored two runs back before having his colours lowered at his latest appearance over 1740m at West Wyalong, beaten 2.5 metres into third after being up on the pace. Won't spend a penny from this draw but luck may play a role on the bell lap. Meets a comparable field and he can play a big role. LETTUCE GO MIKI (1) won at Riverina Paceway two runs ago before finishing fourth at his latest appearance over 1730m at Bathurst, beaten 18 metres. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Certainly cannot be faulted after that last effort. Good enough to put himself back in the winners' stall. A LIL BIT OF LOVE (6) is the next elect off a last-start win by 24 metres at West Wyalong over 1740m. MILLWOOD GRACE NZ (8) has each-way claims off a last-start win by 10 metres at Dubbo over 1720m.",
